-R . kacc

# MM2/: the Church's-Thesis-witness wrapper around
# coq-library-undecidability's own MM2 simulator (see
# Util/MM2_{stepper,embed_nat,simulator}.v and
# Reductions/{FRACTRAN_computable_to_MM2_computable,MM2_Splice}.v for the
# general-purpose MM2 content itself), plus RtcBridge.v, a small piece of
# CKA-specific glue (bridges Coq's clos_refl_trans to stdpp's
# relations.rtc).
MM2/Simulator.v
MM2/RtcBridge.v

# MM2/Legacy/: an earlier, self-contained axiom-free S-M-N-style
# construction directly at the MM2 level, predating and superseded by
# the T_L-based route above (used in the main argument). Not on the
# critical path. Genuinely MM2-generic, no CKA content.
MM2/Legacy/TLUniform_MM2.v
MM2/Legacy/MM2_PrefixSplice.v

# MM2/Legacy/EffectiveInseparability_MM2_Race.v and MM2/Legacy/SMN_MM2.v
# (which Requires it) are excluded here, not deleted. Their
# semidec_of_MM2_computable needs `extract` to compose the
# already-registered mm2_haltedAt_computable/progOf_computable instances
# (now upstream, in Undecidability.MinskyMachines.Util.MM2_simulator)
# across a file boundary; this genuinely fails both via `extract` and via
# plain `typeclasses eauto` -- the same class of MetaRocq cross-file
# extraction-composition limitation documented in MM2_simulator.v's own
# header, but with no colocation fix available here since semidec_of_MM2
# is CKA-project-local, not something to also move upstream. Fixing this
# properly would mean re-deriving the ~150-line extraction chain
# (mm2_atom_fun_computable through mm2_haltedAt_computable) a second
# time, locally, purely for this non-critical-path pair of files.
# MM2/Legacy/EffectiveInseparability_MM2_Race.v
# MM2/Legacy/SMN_MM2.v

# Computability/ no longer exists here: its four files (pure
# effective-inseparability/creative/m-complete theory over an abstract
# numbering, plus T_L/CT_L/EA bridging -- zero MM2 or KA content) live in
# coq-synthetic-computability instead, as
# ReducibilityDegrees/EffectiveInseparabilityCore.v, Models/EA_L.v,
# Models/EA_L_Myhill.v (renamed to avoid colliding with the pre-existing
# Basic/Myhill.v, a different classical result), and Models/T_L_Bridge.v.

